IMPORT prelude

-- Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (Western Australia) -- the apprentice's or trainee's questions: what a
-- training contract is and who signs it (ss 60, 60A, 60E), which qualifications go through one (ss 60C, 60D), when it
-- starts and who must lodge it (s 60F), probation and termination (s 60G), suspension, variation and transfer to another
-- employer (ss 60E(4), 60F(4)), what happens when it ends (ss 60F(6), 60H), completing it and being assessed competent
-- instead (ss 60D(1), 60I), appeals and disputes (ss 60, 60F(8)-(9), 60G(4)-(5)), and the student's questions about a
-- course and a qualification (ss 5, 58A).
--
-- SEAT: the apprentice or trainee -- "the person who is named in a training contract as the person who will be trained
-- under the contract, whether the person is termed an apprentice, a trainee, a cadet, an intern or some other term" (s 60A)
-- -- and the person about to become one, such as a school leaver going to TAFE. Every decision is phrased as that person
-- would ask it: "Is my contract a training contract?", "Has it started?", "May my employer end it?", "Can I be transferred?",
-- "Can I get my ticket without finishing?". Where the Act hands a judgment to someone else -- the chief executive (ss 60E(2),
-- 60F(3)(d), 60G(3)), the Minister (s 60C), a registered training provider (s 60I), the Industrial Relations Commission
-- (ss 60F(9), 60G(5)) -- the answer is conditional on that judgment, asked as a fact.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 5(1) ("approved VET course", "approved VET qualification", "registered training provider",
-- "vocational education and training"), s 58A(1), (3) (who may provide a course and confer a qualification, $10,000),
-- s 60 (what the regulations may do, read for what the Act leaves to them), s 60A ("apprentice", "training contract"),
-- s 60B, s 60C(3), (4), s 60D ($10,000), s 60E, s 60F ($3,000), s 60G ($10,000), s 60H, s 60I.
--
-- Edition: compilation from legislation.wa.gov.au (mrdoc 47549, retrieved 7 September 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_47549.txt. The deposit names no compilation number; its compilation table ends with
-- the Vocational Education and Training Amendment Act 2024 (No. 8 of 2024; s 6, which inserted s 60J, in force 11 July
-- 2024); the last reprint listed is Reprint 2 as at 7 August 2009; the uncommenced provisions table lists only the State
-- Superannuation (Transitional and Consequential Provisions) Act 2000 s 75.
-- Regulations: none deposited. Part 7 leaves almost everything an apprentice meets day to day to regulations under ss 60
-- and 67 (in WA, the Vocational Education and Training (General) Regulations 2009, not deposited and not read): the
-- capacity of a person under 18 to sign, a parent's signature, the form of the contract, the probation period, how and when
-- it is lodged, the grounds for cancelling registration, and how disputes are resolved. Each is asked here as a fact
-- ("the regulations permit it", "the regulations require a parent to sign"), never guessed. The Minister's s 60C
-- classification (published in the Gazette and on the chief executive's register, not deposited) is a fact too.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: Parts 2-6 (the Minister, the State Training Board, the Training Accreditation Council, colleges, other
-- institutions); Part 7A beyond s 58A(1) and (3) (registration of providers and accreditation of courses, from the
-- provider's seat); Part 8A (VET inspectors); Part 8 (miscellaneous, regulations, transitional); s 60C(1), (2), (5)-(7)
-- beyond the classification as a fact; s 60J (delegation). Fees and charges (s 67(2)(b), regulations) are not encoded.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA)`

§§ `5, 58A -- my course and my provider`

-- s 5(1): "approved VET course means a VET course that -- (a) is accredited by the Council under Part 7A; or (b) is
-- accredited under a corresponding law; or (c) is prescribed by the regulations". Whether a course is accredited or
-- prescribed is a fact (the Council's and other States' registers are not deposited). The School Education Act 1999
-- s 11B(1)(b) borrows this definition for a child leaving school in the final two years.
@export Is my course an approved VET course (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 5(1))?
GIVEN `accredited by the Training Accreditation Council` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Training Accreditation Council has accredited the course under Part 7A
      `accredited under a corresponding law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the course is accredited under another State's or Territory's corresponding law
      `prescribed by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations prescribe the course
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my course an approved VET course` IF
       `accredited by the Training Accreditation Council`
    OR `accredited under a corresponding law`
    OR `prescribed by the regulations`

-- s 58A(1): "A person must not claim or purport to provide an approved VET course if -- (a) the person is not a registered
-- training provider; or (b) the person is a registered training provider but is not permitted to provide the course by --
-- (i) any condition of the person's registration ...; or (ii) any condition of the course's accreditation; or (iii) any
-- order of the Council". (2): (1)(a) does not apply to a person providing it "under an arrangement with a registered training
-- provider ... while being monitored by the provider". (3) is the same for conferring a qualification. Penalty $10,000.
-- "registered training provider" (s 5(1)): registered by the Council under Part 7A or under a corresponding law.
DECLARE `My provider` HAS
    `is a registered training provider` IS A BOOLEAN
        -- s 5(1): registered by the Council under Part 7A, or under a corresponding law
    `is permitted by its registration conditions, the accreditation and the Council's orders` IS A BOOLEAN
        -- s 58A(1)(b)(i)-(iii), (3)(b)(i)-(ii)
    `acts for a registered training provider that monitors it` IS A BOOLEAN
        -- s 58A(2): an exception to (1)(a) only

@export May my provider offer me this approved VET course (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 58A(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my provider` IS A `My provider` @desc Who is providing the course, and on what registration
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my provider offer me this course` IF
        (`my provider`'s `is a registered training provider` AND `my provider`'s `is permitted by its registration conditions, the accreditation and the Council's orders`)
    OR  `my provider`'s `acts for a registered training provider that monitors it`

§§ `60A, 60C, 60D -- which qualifications go through a training contract`

-- s 60C(3): the Minister "must classify each prescribed VET qualification ... into one of these 3 classes -- (a) class A
-- qualifications, being qualifications that a person cannot obtain except by fulfilling the obligations of an apprentice
-- under a training contract; (b) class B qualifications, being qualifications that a person may, but need not, obtain by
-- fulfilling the obligations of an apprentice under a training contract; (c) class C qualifications, being qualifications
-- that a person cannot obtain by fulfilling the obligations of an apprentice under a training contract." (4): the
-- classification "does not limit the operation of Division 3" (being assessed competent). An "approved VET qualification"
-- (s 5(1)) is any other certificate of an approved VET course. The class of a qualification is the Minister's, a fact.
DECLARE `Qualification class` IS ONE OF
    `class A`                                  -- s 60C(3)(a): only through a training contract (or Division 3)
    `class B`                                  -- s 60C(3)(b): through a training contract or otherwise
    `class C`                                  -- s 60C(3)(c): never through a training contract
    `an approved VET qualification`            -- s 5(1): not a prescribed VET qualification

GIVEN `the class` IS A `Qualification class`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is class A or class B` IF
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `class A` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `class B` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 60D(2): "An employer must not enter into a training contract with an employee under which the employee is to be trained
-- in order to obtain a prescribed VET qualification unless the qualification is a class A or class B qualification." And
-- s 60E(1)(a)(i), (3)(a): a training contract can only be for a class A or B qualification.
@export May my employer put me on a training contract for this qualification (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) ss 60D(2), 60E(1), (3))?
GIVEN `the class` IS A `Qualification class` @desc How the Minister has classified the qualification
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my employer put me on a training contract for it` IF
    `is class A or class B` `the class`

-- s 60D(3): "An employer must not agree to train an employee for the purpose of the employee obtaining a class A or class B
-- qualification except under a training contract." Penalty $10,000.
@export May my employer train me for this qualification without a training contract (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60D(3))?
GIVEN `the class` IS A `Qualification class` @desc How the Minister has classified the qualification
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my employer train me for it without a training contract` IF
    NOT (`is class A or class B` `the class`)

-- How each kind of qualification can be had. s 60C(3) for the training contract; s 60D(1) and s 60I(1) for class A
-- ("as a result of training received from an employer and other learning"); s 60I(2), (3), (4) for the rest (assessment
-- without completing an approved course). Completing an approved VET course: the class B, C and approved qualifications
-- are certificates of one (s 5(1); s 60I(2)(c), (3), (4) assume the course route); a class A one "cannot" be had except by
-- the contract (s 60C(3)(a)) or Division 3 (s 60C(4), s 60D(1)(b)), so a course alone does not give it (an inference from
-- "cannot obtain except").
DECLARE Route IS ONE OF
    `completing a registered training contract`
    `completing an approved VET course`
    `being assessed competent, after training with an employer`
    `being assessed competent, without training from an employer`

@export Can I get this qualification this way (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) ss 60C(3), (4), 60D(1), 60I)?
GIVEN `the class` IS A `Qualification class` @desc How the Minister has classified the qualification
      `the route` IS A Route @desc The way you would get the qualification
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I get this qualification this way` IF
    CONSIDER `the route`
    WHEN `completing a registered training contract` THEN `is class A or class B` `the class`
    WHEN `completing an approved VET course` THEN
        CONSIDER `the class`
        WHEN `class A` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE
    WHEN `being assessed competent, after training with an employer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `being assessed competent, without training from an employer` THEN
        CONSIDER `the class`
        WHEN `class A` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `60A, 60E -- what my training contract is`

-- s 60E(1): "A training contract is a contract under which -- (a) a person who is or will be an employer agrees the
-- following -- (i) that a person who is or will be an employee will be employed while he or she fulfils the requirements of
-- the contract in order to obtain a class A or class B qualification; (ii) to train the employee in accordance with the
-- contract; (iii) to permit the employee to fulfil his or her obligations under the contract and to be trained and assessed
-- in accordance with the contract; (iv) that any time spent by the employee in performing his or her obligations under the
-- contract and in being trained and assessed under the contract, whether at the employer's workplace or not, is to be taken
-- for all purposes (including the payment of remuneration) to be time spent working for the employer; and (b) the employee
-- agrees to fulfil his or her obligations under the contract and to be trained and assessed in accordance with the
-- contract." (2): "With the approval of the chief executive, 2 or more employers may enter into a training contract with one
-- apprentice." (3): it "must (a) state the class A or class B qualification to which the contract relates; (b) comply with
-- the regulations and with any requirements imposed under the regulations".
-- s 60A: "training contract means a contract that complies with section 60E". So a contract lacking any limb is not one.
-- Reading (2) as a condition (more than one employer only with approval) is an inference from "may ... with the approval".
DECLARE `My contract` HAS
    `an employer agrees I will be employed while I fulfil it to obtain the qualification` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 60E(1)(a)(i)
    `my employer agrees to train me under it` IS A BOOLEAN                                             -- (a)(ii)
    `my employer agrees to let me fulfil my obligations and be trained and assessed` IS A BOOLEAN      -- (a)(iii)
    `my employer agrees my training and assessment time is working time, including for pay` IS A BOOLEAN -- (a)(iv)
    `I agree to fulfil my obligations and to be trained and assessed` IS A BOOLEAN                     -- (b)
    `it states the qualification` IS A BOOLEAN                                                         -- (3)(a)
    `the class of that qualification` IS A `Qualification class`                                       -- (1)(a)(i), (3)(a)
    `it complies with the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN                                                    -- (3)(b): a fact
    `the number of employers` IS A NUMBER                                                              -- (2)
    `the chief executive approved more than one employer` IS A BOOLEAN                                 -- (2)

@export Is my contract a training contract (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) ss 60A, 60E(1)-(3))?
GIVEN `my contract` IS A `My contract` @desc What your contract says and who has signed it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my contract a training contract` IF
        `my contract`'s `an employer agrees I will be employed while I fulfil it to obtain the qualification`
    AND `my contract`'s `my employer agrees to train me under it`
    AND `my contract`'s `my employer agrees to let me fulfil my obligations and be trained and assessed`
    AND `my contract`'s `my employer agrees my training and assessment time is working time, including for pay`
    AND `my contract`'s `I agree to fulfil my obligations and to be trained and assessed`
    AND `my contract`'s `it states the qualification`
    AND `is class A or class B` (`my contract`'s `the class of that qualification`)
    AND `my contract`'s `it complies with the regulations`
    AND (    `my contract`'s `the number of employers` AT MOST 1
         OR  `my contract`'s `the chief executive approved more than one employer`)

-- s 60A: "apprentice means the person who is named in a training contract as the person who will be trained under the
-- contract, whether the person is termed an apprentice, a trainee, a cadet, an intern or some other term". A student on a
-- course with no employer has no training contract and is not an apprentice under this Act.
@export Am I an apprentice under Part 7 (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60A)?
GIVEN `my contract` IS A `My contract` @desc What your contract says and who has signed it
      `I am named in it as the person to be trained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract names you as the person who will be trained under it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an apprentice under Part 7` IF
    `Is my contract a training contract` `my contract` AND `I am named in it as the person to be trained`

-- s 60E(1)(a)(iv): time training and being assessed, "whether at the employer's workplace or not", is "to be taken for all
-- purposes (including the payment of remuneration) to be time spent working for the employer". It is a limb of every
-- training contract, so it holds wherever the contract is one.
DECLARE `Where I am training` IS ONE OF
    `at my employer's workplace`
    `away from the workplace, such as at TAFE`

@export Does my training time count as working time, including for pay (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60E(1)(a)(iv))?
GIVEN `my contract` IS A `My contract` @desc What your contract says and who has signed it
      `where` IS A `Where I am training` @desc Where you are being trained or assessed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my training time count as working time` IF
    `Is my contract a training contract` `my contract`

-- Who signs. s 60E(1): the parties are the employer (or, with approval, employers: (2)) and the employee. The Act says
-- nothing more: s 60(c) lets the regulations "give persons under 18 years of age the capacity to enter into training
-- contracts", and s 60(b) lets them "provide for the content or form" of the contract, which is where any parent's or
-- guardian's signature would come from. Neither regulation is deposited, so both are facts. A person of 18 or over needs
-- no help from the regulations (an inference: the Act's only provision about age is s 60(c)).
@export Can I sign my training contract on my own (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) ss 60(b), (c), 60E(1))?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years when you sign
      `the regulations give a person my age capacity to sign` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations under s 60(c) give a person under 18 of your age capacity to enter into a training contract
      `the regulations require a parent or guardian to sign too` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations on the form of the contract require a parent or guardian of a person your age to sign as well
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I sign my training contract on my own` IF
        `my age` AT LEAST 18
    OR  (    `the regulations give a person my age capacity to sign`
         AND (NOT `the regulations require a parent or guardian to sign too`))

-- s 60B: "If a provision of this Part or of regulations made under section 60 is inconsistent with a provision of the
-- Industrial Relations Act 1979 or any order, award or industrial agreement in force under that Act, the former provision
-- prevails." Whether there is an inconsistency is a fact.
DECLARE `Which prevails` IS ONE OF
    `Part 7 and its regulations prevail over the award`
    `no conflict: both apply`

@export Which prevails, Part 7 or my award (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60B)?
GIVEN `they are inconsistent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a provision of Part 7 or its regulations is inconsistent with your award, industrial agreement or the Industrial Relations Act 1979
GIVETH A `Which prevails`
`Which prevails, Part 7 or my award` MEANS
    IF `they are inconsistent`
    THEN `Part 7 and its regulations prevail over the award`
    ELSE `no conflict: both apply`

§§ `60F -- registration: when my contract starts`

-- s 60F(1): "A training contract does not commence until it is registered by the chief executive under this section."
@export Has my training contract started (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60F(1))?
GIVEN `the chief executive has registered it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the chief executive has registered your training contract
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my training contract started` IF
    `the chief executive has registered it`

-- s 60F(3): "The chief executive may refuse to register a training contract -- (a) if the contract was not lodged in
-- accordance with the regulations; or (b) if a requirement for the contract imposed under section 60C(5) has not been
-- complied with; or (c) if the content or form of the contract does not comply with the regulations; or (d) if the chief
-- executive is satisfied the employer is not able to train the apprentice adequately or is not a fit and proper person to
-- enter into the contract; or (e) if the apprentice is ineligible under the regulations to enter into the contract; or (f)
-- for any reason prescribed in the regulations." (4): the same for a variation. "May refuse": a ground permits refusal, it
-- does not compel it; with no ground, refusal is not open.
DECLARE `My lodgement` HAS
    `it was lodged in accordance with the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN                                         -- (3)(a)
    `the Minister's section 60C(5) requirements were met` IS A BOOLEAN                                      -- (3)(b)
    `its content and form comply with the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN                                         -- (3)(c)
    `the chief executive is satisfied my employer cannot train me adequately or is not fit and proper` IS A BOOLEAN -- (3)(d)
    `I am ineligible under the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN                                                    -- (3)(e)
    `a reason prescribed in the regulations applies` IS A BOOLEAN                                           -- (3)(f)

@export May the chief executive refuse to register my training contract (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60F(3), (4))?
GIVEN `my lodgement` IS A `My lodgement` @desc How your contract was lodged and what the chief executive has found
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my contract be refused registration` IF
       (NOT `my lodgement`'s `it was lodged in accordance with the regulations`)
    OR (NOT `my lodgement`'s `the Minister's section 60C(5) requirements were met`)
    OR (NOT `my lodgement`'s `its content and form comply with the regulations`)
    OR `my lodgement`'s `the chief executive is satisfied my employer cannot train me adequately or is not fit and proper`
    OR `my lodgement`'s `I am ineligible under the regulations`
    OR `my lodgement`'s `a reason prescribed in the regulations applies`

-- s 60F(2): "An employer who enters into a training contract must lodge it with the chief executive in accordance with the
-- regulations for registration. Penalty: a fine of $3 000." The duty is the employer's, not the apprentice's.
DECLARE Party IS ONE OF
    `me, the apprentice`
    `my employer`

@export Who must lodge my training contract for registration (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60F(2))?
GIVETH A Party
DECIDE `Who must lodge my training contract` IS `my employer`

§§ `60E(4), 60F(4) -- suspending, varying and transferring my contract`

-- s 60E(4): "Subject to the regulations, a training contract -- (a) may be varied by the parties; and (b) may be suspended
-- by a party; and (c) may be assigned by the employer to another person who employs the apprentice." s 60F(4): a variation
-- must be lodged and may be refused registration like the contract itself. "By the parties" is read as all of them
-- together, "by a party" as either one alone (an inference from the contrast).
DECLARE Change IS ONE OF
    `a variation`
    `a suspension`
    `a transfer to another employer`

DECLARE `Who may make it` IS ONE OF
    `my employer and I together`
    `either my employer or I, alone`
    `my employer alone, to another person who employs me`

@export Who may make this change to my training contract (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60E(4))?
GIVEN `the change` IS A Change @desc The change to your training contract
GIVETH A `Who may make it`
`Who may make this change` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the change`
    WHEN `a variation` THEN `my employer and I together`
    WHEN `a suspension` THEN `either my employer or I, alone`
    WHEN `a transfer to another employer` THEN `my employer alone, to another person who employs me`

-- s 60E(4)(c): assignment is "by the employer" and only "to another person who employs the apprentice", "subject to the
-- regulations". The Act does not require the apprentice's consent to the assignment; that the new employer must employ the
-- apprentice means the apprentice must have become that person's employee.
@export May my training contract be transferred to this new employer (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60E(4)(c))?
GIVEN `my current employer assigns it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is your current employer who assigns the contract
      `the new employer employs me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person it is assigned to employs you
      `the regulations permit it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations allow this assignment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my contract be transferred to this employer` IF
    `my current employer assigns it` AND `the new employer employs me` AND `the regulations permit it`

@export May I suspend my training contract (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60E(4)(b))?
GIVEN `the regulations permit it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations allow the suspension
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I suspend my training contract` IF
    `the regulations permit it`

@export Must this change be lodged with the chief executive for registration (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60F(4))?
GIVEN `the change` IS A Change @desc The change to your training contract
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must this change be lodged for registration` IF
    CONSIDER `the change`
    WHEN `a variation` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `60G -- probation and termination`

-- s 60G(1): "Subject to the regulations, a party to a training contract may terminate it." (2): "An employer who is a party
-- to a training contract the probation period of which (if any) has expired must not terminate the contract unless -- (a)
-- the apprentice has consented to the termination; or (b) the chief executive has approved the termination. Penalty: a fine
-- of $10 000." The length of any probation period is set by the regulations or the contract, not the Act (a fact).
-- "(if any)": read so that a contract with no probation period is protected from the start (an inference; the other
-- reading would leave a contract with no probation period never protected, which the words do not suggest).
@export Am I protected from my employer ending my contract without my consent (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60G(2))?
GIVEN `my contract has a probation period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your contract has a probation period
      `the probation period has expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that probation period has ended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I protected from termination without my consent` IF
    (NOT `my contract has a probation period`) OR `the probation period has expired`

DECLARE `My termination` HAS
    `the regulations permit it` IS A BOOLEAN                   -- s 60G(1): "subject to the regulations"
    `my contract has a probation period` IS A BOOLEAN          -- s 60G(2)
    `the probation period has expired` IS A BOOLEAN            -- s 60G(2)
    `I consented` IS A BOOLEAN                                 -- s 60G(2)(a)
    `the chief executive approved it` IS A BOOLEAN             -- s 60G(2)(b)

GIVEN `who` IS A Party
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is my employer` IF
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `my employer` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@export May my training contract be terminated by this party (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60G(1), (2))?
GIVEN `who` IS A Party @desc Who is ending the contract
      `the termination` IS A `My termination` @desc The facts about the termination
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my contract be terminated` IF
        `the termination`'s `the regulations permit it`
    AND (    (NOT (`is my employer` `who`))
         OR  (NOT (`Am I protected from termination without my consent` (`the termination`'s `my contract has a probation period`) (`the termination`'s `the probation period has expired`)))
         OR  `the termination`'s `I consented`
         OR  `the termination`'s `the chief executive approved it`)

-- s 60G(2) is an offence by the employer, whatever the regulations say: termination after probation without consent or
-- approval.
@export Has my employer committed an offence by ending my contract (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60G(2))?
GIVEN `the termination` IS A `My termination` @desc The facts about your employer ending the contract
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my employer committed an offence by ending my contract` IF
        `Am I protected from termination without my consent` (`the termination`'s `my contract has a probation period`) (`the termination`'s `the probation period has expired`)
    AND (NOT `the termination`'s `I consented`)
    AND (NOT `the termination`'s `the chief executive approved it`)

-- s 60G(3): "The chief executive must approve the termination of a training contract under subsection (2) if satisfied --
-- (a) the employer has ceased or is about to cease business; or (b) the employer is unable to fulfil the employer's
-- obligations under the contract due to a substantial change of circumstances that has occurred since the contract was
-- entered into; or (c) the apprentice has engaged in serious misconduct; or (d) as to any matter prescribed, but otherwise
-- may refuse to approve the termination." The chief executive's satisfaction is the condition; it is not decided here.
DECLARE `My employer's reason` IS ONE OF
    `my employer has ceased or is about to cease business`
    `a substantial change of circumstances since signing means my employer cannot fulfil the contract`
    `I have engaged in serious misconduct`
    `a matter prescribed by the regulations`
    `some other reason`

DECLARE `What the chief executive must do` IS ONE OF
    `must approve the termination, if satisfied the reason exists`
    `may refuse to approve the termination`

@export What must the chief executive do when my employer asks to end my contract (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60G(3))?
GIVEN `the reason` IS A `My employer's reason` @desc The reason your employer gives for ending the contract
GIVETH A `What the chief executive must do`
`What must the chief executive do` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reason`
    WHEN `some other reason` THEN `may refuse to approve the termination`
    OTHERWISE `must approve the termination, if satisfied the reason exists`

§§ `60F(5)-(6), 60H -- when my contract ends`

-- s 60F(5): the chief executive "may cancel the registration of a training contract for any reason prescribed in the
-- regulations". (6): "If the chief executive cancels the registration of a training contract, the contract ceases to have
-- effect." s 60H(1): "If a training contract ceases to have effect, whether under section 60F(6) or because it is terminated
-- or expires or for any other reason, the employment of the apprentice by the employer under the contract ceases." (2): that
-- "does not prevent the parties entering into another employment agreement or arrangement".
DECLARE `My contract's status` HAS
    `it has been registered` IS A BOOLEAN          -- s 60F(1)
    `its registration has been cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 60F(6)
    `it has been terminated` IS A BOOLEAN          -- s 60G, s 60H(1)
    `it has expired` IS A BOOLEAN                  -- s 60H(1)

@export Is my training contract in effect (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) ss 60F(1), (6), 60H(1))?
GIVEN `the status` IS A `My contract's status` @desc What has happened to your contract
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my training contract in effect` IF
        `the status`'s `it has been registered`
    AND (NOT `the status`'s `its registration has been cancelled`)
    AND (NOT `the status`'s `it has been terminated`)
    AND (NOT `the status`'s `it has expired`)

-- s 60H(1): the employment "under the contract" ceases with it. Before registration the contract has not commenced, and
-- whether the person is employed otherwise is not a question this Act answers.
@export Am I still employed under my training contract (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60H)?
GIVEN `the status` IS A `My contract's status` @desc What has happened to your contract
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I still employed under my training contract` IF
    `Is my training contract in effect` `the status`

@export May my employer and I agree a new employment arrangement after my training contract ends (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60H(2))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May we agree a new arrangement after it ends` IS TRUE

-- s 60F(5): cancellation only "for any reason prescribed in the regulations" (a fact).
@export May the chief executive cancel my contract's registration (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60F(5))?
GIVEN `a prescribed reason applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reason prescribed in the regulations for cancelling registration applies
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my contract's registration be cancelled` IF
    `a prescribed reason applies`

§§ `60D(1), 60I -- finishing: getting my qualification`

-- s 60D(1): "A registered training provider must not confer, or offer or purport to confer, a class A qualification on a
-- person unless -- (a) the person has fulfilled the obligations of an apprentice under a training contract that was
-- registered under Division 2; or (b) the person has satisfied the registered training provider under Division 3."
-- s 60I(1): a class A qualification to a person who has not entered a contract, "or has entered into such a contract as an
-- apprentice but has only partly fulfilled the apprentice's obligations under it", "if, after assessing the person, the
-- provider is satisfied the person nevertheless has, as a result of training received from an employer and other learning,
-- the skills and competency required". (2)-(4): class B, class C and approved qualifications on assessment, without the
-- employer-training condition. s 58A(3): only a registered training provider permitted by its registration and the
-- Council's orders may confer any of them. All "subject to the regulations" (not deposited).
DECLARE `My completion` HAS
    `I fulfilled my obligations under a registered training contract` IS A BOOLEAN           -- s 60D(1)(a)
    `I completed an approved VET course for it` IS A BOOLEAN                                 -- s 5(1)
    `my provider assessed me and is satisfied I have the skills and competency` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 60I
    `my skills come from training with an employer and other learning` IS A BOOLEAN          -- s 60I(1), class A only

@export May my training provider confer this qualification on me (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) ss 58A(3), 60D(1), 60I)?
GIVEN `the class` IS A `Qualification class` @desc How the Minister has classified the qualification
      `my provider` IS A `My provider` @desc The provider that would confer it
      `my completion` IS A `My completion` @desc What you have done towards the qualification
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my provider confer this qualification` IF
        `my provider`'s `is a registered training provider`
    AND `my provider`'s `is permitted by its registration conditions, the accreditation and the Council's orders`
    AND `I have met the qualification's route` `the class` `my completion`
    WHERE
        GIVEN `c` IS A `Qualification class`
              `done` IS A `My completion`
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        `I have met the qualification's route` `c` `done` MEANS
            CONSIDER `c`
            WHEN `class A` THEN
                    `done`'s `I fulfilled my obligations under a registered training contract`
                OR  (`done`'s `my provider assessed me and is satisfied I have the skills and competency` AND `done`'s `my skills come from training with an employer and other learning`)
            WHEN `class B` THEN
                    `done`'s `I fulfilled my obligations under a registered training contract`
                OR  `done`'s `I completed an approved VET course for it`
                OR  `done`'s `my provider assessed me and is satisfied I have the skills and competency`
            OTHERWISE
                    `done`'s `I completed an approved VET course for it`
                OR  `done`'s `my provider assessed me and is satisfied I have the skills and competency`

§§ `60, 60F(8)-(9), 60G(4)-(5) -- appeals and disputes`

-- s 60F(8): "A person who is dissatisfied by a decision made by the chief executive under this section may appeal against
-- it to the Western Australian Industrial Relations Commission." s 60G(4): the same for a decision under s 60G. A
-- provider's refusal of a qualification is appealable only if the regulations confer a right (s 60(i)): a fact.
DECLARE Decision IS ONE OF
    `the chief executive refusing to register my contract`
    `the chief executive refusing to register a variation`
    `the chief executive cancelling my contract's registration`
    `the chief executive approving my employer's termination`
    `the chief executive refusing to approve a termination`
    `a training provider refusing me a qualification`

@export May I appeal this decision to the Western Australian Industrial Relations Commission (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) ss 60(i), 60F(8), 60G(4))?
GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision @desc The decision you are dissatisfied with
      `the regulations give an appeal against refusing a qualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations under s 60(i) give a right of appeal against refusing a qualification
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I appeal to the Commission` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `a training provider refusing me a qualification` THEN `the regulations give an appeal against refusing a qualification`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 60F(9), s 60G(5): "the Commission must rehear the matter and may confirm the decision or set it aside and either
-- substitute a decision the chief executive could make or order the chief executive to decide the matter again." Nothing
-- in the Act lets the Commission award compensation or fine anyone on such an appeal.
DECLARE `Appeal outcome` IS ONE OF
    `confirm the decision`
    `set it aside and substitute a decision the chief executive could make`
    `set it aside and order the chief executive to decide again`
    `award me compensation`
    `fine my employer`

@export May the Commission do this on my appeal (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) ss 60F(9), 60G(5))?
GIVEN `the outcome` IS AN `Appeal outcome` @desc What you want the Commission to do
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Commission do this on my appeal` IF
    CONSIDER `the outcome`
    WHEN `award me compensation` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `fine my employer` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 60(f): the regulations may, "in relation to disputes arising under training contracts between the parties to them --
-- (i) provide for their resolution, including by the chief executive or a person appointed by the chief executive; (ii)
-- confer on any such party aggrieved by a decision ... a right of appeal to the Western Australian Industrial Relations
-- Commission." The Act sets up no forum itself; what the regulations provide is a fact.
DECLARE `Where my dispute goes` IS ONE OF
    `to the chief executive or an appointee, then on appeal to the Industrial Relations Commission`
    `to the chief executive or an appointee, with no appeal under the Act`
    `the Act and its regulations set up no forum for it`

@export Where can I take a dispute with my employer under my training contract (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) s 60(f))?
GIVEN `the regulations provide for resolution by the chief executive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations provide for the chief executive (or an appointee) to resolve disputes under training contracts
      `the regulations give an appeal to the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations give a party aggrieved by that decision an appeal to the Industrial Relations Commission
GIVETH A `Where my dispute goes`
`Where can I take my dispute` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the regulations provide for resolution by the chief executive`) THEN `the Act and its regulations set up no forum for it`
        IF `the regulations give an appeal to the Commission` THEN `to the chief executive or an appointee, then on appeal to the Industrial Relations Commission`
        OTHERWISE `to the chief executive or an appointee, with no appeal under the Act`

§§ `penalties`

-- s 58A: $10,000; s 60D: $10,000; s 60F(2): $3,000; s 60G(2): $10,000.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `providing a course or conferring a qualification without being permitted (s 58A)`
    `training me for a class A or B qualification outside a training contract (s 60D(3))`
    `putting me on a training contract for a class C qualification (s 60D(2))`
    `failing to lodge my training contract (s 60F(2))`
    `ending my training contract after probation without consent or approval (s 60G(2))`

@export What is the most the offender can be fined, in dollars (Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) ss 58A, 60D, 60F(2), 60G(2))?
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence @desc The offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most the offender can be fined` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `failing to lodge my training contract (s 60F(2))` THEN 3000
    OTHERWISE 10000
